{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline","id":958831,"title":"Somatics: A single physical discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-27T12:20:25-07:00","id":958831,"title":"Somatics: A single physical discipline","content":"So, I know some (at least I am) are unimpressed by the new physical disciplines. Sure, they're better than they were in 1st edition, but still require improving in a linear fashion by spending dots one after another to improve the singular effect (well, several different effects, but always the same ones). It's still less impressive than most other options you could spend your Experience on.<br /> <br /> I decided, as such, to create <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1574pK3GjlPao6Tf3UnYXH1xwcCsfeXa_NgBZrfOu7AY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Somatics</a>, a single physical discipline which provides all the benefits of the three physical disciplines and then some, making Kindred that buy it more physically powerful than they'd otherwise be. It's a little potent, as even the individual powers get a slight boost in some cases, to last longer, but the idea is that it makes Kindred more of a physical force by default. I also snuck in a flight type ability, too, but made it more limited than, say, using Protean to fly long-term as a bat.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm open to input, keeping in mind it's MEANT to be pretty potent. Still, I'm considering if maybe I want to switch Aviation and Celerity around, depending how potent people think the ability to fly and a Dex increase is, compared to Celerity's fairly large improvements.<br /> <br /> In case it need be said, if you don't think the physical disciplines are underpowered, then that's your right to think, but this thread isn't meant for you, just don't use the discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:08:00-07:00","id":958858,"title":"","content":"What are you fighting that makes you think Kindred are not powerhouse physical monsters? They naturally take bashing from almost all sources of damage, and then heal it right back up in no time. They have physical intensity, do not fall unconscious from bashing, never tire, and are immune to nearly all forms of toxin. And that's all without Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:31:59-07:00","id":958869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958858#post958858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you fighting that makes you think Kindred are not powerhouse physical monsters? They naturally take bashing from almost all sources of damage, and then heal it right back up in no time. They have physical intensity, do not fall unconscious from bashing, never tire, and are immune to nearly all forms of toxin. And that's all without Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said their default abilities aren't good, I said I wanted the physical disciplines to be better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:58:19-07:00","id":958901,"title":"","content":"Celerity is arguably the best discipline in the game( it's been said by multiple people in multiple threads) I do not wish to be rude, but if you do not think they are powerful enough physically, but perhaps is it that you are not using them correctly?<br /> <br /> Base Vigor gives STR, I can see if you think that is the only thing it does then it would be very good compared to the rest<br /> Or even Base Resilience just gives stamina, but spending vitae increases their usefulness 10 fold...<br /> <br /> say you had 5 vigor, and 1 strength and 1 weaponry 1 brawl or whatever. Spend 1 vitae and you are going to auto deal +5 damage on a hit. so say you got 1 success you are dealing 6+ damage. You could call shot stake through a heart and down a vampire in 1 hit with 1 vitae.<br /> <br /> 5 celerity you could pretty much interrupt their turn every time and get 5 turns in a row with them missing or whatever. if you are using it to fight you should be able to kill your opponent in 5 turns.. Or get half way across the country.<br /> <br /> 5 resilience you can down grade so much damage you would barely be hurt after a bomb exploding next to you..<br /> <br /> How are these not good *enough*? they are extremely powerful, what is your reason to make them better? I know you said you feel that they are underpowered but Underpowered as compared to what? or Why are they underpowered?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you be comfortable taking Majesty, Dominate and Nightmare and making them 1 Discipline that gives you all the effects of all 3? I honestly believe taking all the effects of 3 disciplines and smashing them into 3 dots is way way too overpowered for any game. It would unbalance everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> For your celerity (3rd dot) you would have to spend 3 vitae to multiply their speed by 4. To do that in 1 turn you would have to have BP 3 to spend 3 vitae in a turn. Where as if I had Celerity 3 normally I would only have to spend 1 vitae. So your power is literally less powerful than the original one. However it is for the entire scene and no one would ever be able to lay a hand on this character. No story teller would be able to touch it in a battle. You could attack your opponent, move 400feet away, they couldnt hit you ( or likely have a LOS to shoot you ) move 400 feet back and hit them again then go first and move 400 feet away again.<br /> <br /> Your resilience I think is over powered compared to the other discplines. You spend 5 vitae and have 5 armor for the rest of the scene against all attacks all the time? there are devotions that cost tons of exp to make you unstoppable for a short time... this pretty much makes you unstoppable period.<br /> <br /> Could you imagine a character spending 5 vitae to carry a truck down the street, and swing it into the cafe, then continue to do so as the people ran out the door? Giving a character +damage on every single hit for an entire scene is.... unbalanced.<br /> <br /> I also dont think it would be very fair or balanced to allow your character to have +5 str, +5 defense. +5stamina, +5 dexterity, double healing and Protean 3 ( ability to fly ) for 15 exp. When it would take everyone else 55 ( unless you were a Daeva 50 )-- counting protean +9-12 more<br /> <br /> You pretty much made a god in 15 exp. When you create your own disciplines and such you need to make sure that they dont break the game. I strongly believe this would. I dont even think a pack of werewolves could take this thing down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-27-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:19:22-07:00","id":958913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958901#post958901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity is arguably the best discipline in the game( it's been said by multiple people in multiple threads) I do not wish to be rude, but if you do not think they are powerful enough physically, but perhaps is it that you are not using them correctly?<br /> <br /> Base Vigor gives STR, I can see if you think that is the only thing it does then it would be very good compared to the rest<br /> Or even Base Resilience just gives stamina, but spending vitae increases their usefulness 10 fold...<br /> <br /> say you had 5 vigor, and 1 strength and 1 weaponry 1 brawl or whatever. Spend 1 vitae and you are going to auto deal +5 damage on a hit. so say you got 1 success you are dealing 6+ damage. You could call shot stake through a heart and down a vampire in 1 hit with 1 vitae.<br /> <br /> 5 celerity you could pretty much interrupt their turn every time and get 5 turns in a row with them missing or whatever. if you are using it to fight you should be able to kill your opponent in 5 turns.. Or get half way across the country.<br /> <br /> 5 resilience you can down grade so much damage you would barely be hurt after a bomb exploding next to you..<br /> <br /> How are these not good *enough*? they are extremely powerful, what is your reason to make them better? I know you said you feel that they are underpowered but Underpowered as compared to what? or Why are they underpowered?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you be comfortable taking Majesty, Dominate and Nightmare and making them 1 Discipline that gives you all the effects of all 3? I honestly believe taking all the effects of 3 disciplines and smashing them into 3 dots is way way too overpowered for any game. It would unbalance everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> For your celerity (3rd dot) you would have to spend 3 vitae to multiply their speed by 4. To do that in 1 turn you would have to have BP 3 to spend 3 vitae in a turn. Where as if I had Celerity 3 normally I would only have to spend 1 vitae. So your power is literally less powerful than the original one. However it is for the entire scene and no one would ever be able to lay a hand on this character. No story teller would be able to touch it in a battle. You could attack your opponent, move 400feet away, they couldnt hit you ( or likely have a LOS to shoot you ) move 400 feet back and hit them again then go first and move 400 feet away again.<br /> <br /> Your resilience I think is over powered compared to the other discplines. You spend 5 vitae and have 5 armor for the rest of the scene against all attacks all the time? there are devotions that cost tons of exp to make you unstoppable for a short time... this pretty much makes you unstoppable period.<br /> <br /> Could you imagine a character spending 5 vitae to carry a truck down the street, and swing it into the cafe, then continue to do so as the people ran out the door? Giving a character +damage on every single hit for an entire scene is.... unbalanced.<br /> <br /> I also dont think it would be very fair or balanced to allow your character to have +5 str, +5 defense. +5stamina, +5 dexterity, double healing and Protean 3 ( ability to fly ) for 15 exp. When it would take everyone else 55 ( unless you were a Daeva 50 )-- counting protean +9-12 more<br /> <br /> You pretty much made a god in 15 exp. When you create your own disciplines and such you need to make sure that they dont break the game. I strongly believe this would. I dont even think a pack of werewolves could take this thing down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first of all:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In case it need be said, if you don't think the physical disciplines are underpowered, then that's your right to think, but this thread isn't meant for you, just don't use the discipline. </div> </div> </div>I'm not otherwise going to respond to the bit about the physical disciplines being underpowered or not normally.<br /> <br /> But as to the gripes about the discipline itself otherwise, which are a bit more on topic:<br /> <br /> I don't think multiplying speed is as good as you seem to think it is. For one thing, using this casually is a masquerade breech, it's not something you'd use in a street brawl or something. But yes, it does provide a significant advantage if dealing with a supernatural threat (or if this is a supernatural enemy that doesn't care), if they only have melee abilities and lack Celerity of their own, or something equivalent (even if the rating is less, they can always interrupt you as you approach). As mentioned, though, it does cost more vitae in exchange for getting to use it for longer.<br /> <br /> Still, I can maybe see what you mean when it comes to Vigor and Resilience. Perhaps I'll change them to work the same way as the 4th dot currently does and have it be 1 Vitae and last for Somatics turns instead of the whole scene, which is a bit better than now, but a fair bit more controllable. But I mean, Resilience is underpowered currently because most powers that grant Armor do it for a scene at a time.<br /> <br /> As for the passive bonuses, I guess it does add up pretty quickly. Perhaps what I can do is make it so you have a pool of 'passive attributes (and defense)' equal to the discipline rating, and then you can allocate it to the choices you have based on the level of the discipline you currently have (and can change it per turn)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:48:09-07:00","id":958926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958913#post958913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, first of all:<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not otherwise going to respond to the bit about the physical disciplines being underpowered or not normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked for thoughts. I gave thoughts. To help you come up with balanced ideas... I would need to know the logic behind WHY you want to do this or WHY you dont think it's good enough. I have seen people on these threads want to change something when they dont even know how it actually works. Which is why I asked ...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958913#post958913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IBut as to the gripes about the discipline itself otherwise, which are a bit more on topic:<br /> <br /> I don't think multiplying speed is as good as you seem to think it is. For one thing, using this casually is a masquerade breech, it's not something you'd use in a street brawl or something. But yes, it does provide a significant advantage if dealing with a supernatural threat (or if this is a supernatural enemy that doesn't care), if they only have melee abilities and lack Celerity of their own, or something equivalent (even if the rating is less, they can always interrupt you as you approach). As mentioned, though, it does cost more vitae in exchange for getting to use it for longer.<br /> <br /> Still, I can maybe see what you mean when it comes to Vigor and Resilience. Perhaps I'll change them to work the same way as the 4th dot currently does and have it be 1 Vitae and last for Somatics turns instead of the whole scene, which is a bit better than now, but a fair bit more controllable. But I mean, Resilience is underpowered currently because most powers that grant Armor do it for a scene at a time.<br /> <br /> As for the passive bonuses, I guess it does add up pretty quickly. Perhaps what I can do is make it so you have a pool of 'passive attributes (and defense)' equal to the discipline rating, and then you can allocate it to the choices you have based on the level of the discipline you currently have (and can change it per turn)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Celerity in a street brawl would not be a masquerade breech as you literally move so fast the other people cant see you doing it. Perhaps if someone looked at some footage after.. oh wait, cant see a vampire on camera. it gives you a huge advantage in a foot chase, dodging attacks, ect. Being able to interrupt someone's action is huge.<br /> <br /> All the other ones give you a totally of 5 some where. I do not think yours should add any more than 5 total. perhaps if you spent it for celerity for the scene then 5 to defense for that scene. but not the other ones.. But it still does give you everything it would cost a normal vampire 50-55 exp+ 9-12xp depending on clans.<br /> <br /> As a story teller I would never be ok with something that would take someone else so much to achieve. If you would allow someone to take majesty, dominate, and nightmare and smash them into one, I would allow this But if you said no way to those 3. then why do you say yes to this one?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:59:22-07:00","id":958932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958926#post958926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You asked for thoughts. I gave thoughts. To help you come up with balanced ideas... I would need to know the logic behind WHY you want to do this or WHY you dont think it's good enough. I have seen people on these threads want to change something when they dont even know how it actually works. Which is why I asked ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, well, the basic idea is that every other discipline gives you 5 powers with their own uses, and each one is more potent than the last. The physical ones give you one power that gets better in a linear fashion with each dot, and a lot of them are underpowered even if you take it at a basis of, say, being the third dot of an unnamed discipline, in my opinion. Yes, +3 stamina is decent, but gaining 3 armor for 1 turn? That's very underwhelming to me.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that the comparison isn't wholly internal; I'm also comparing to other gamelines (I can't help it). Celerity is alright in the context of vampire, but is outclassed entirely by a werewolf in urhan, who can interrupt an unlimited number of times (if they have essence), for instance. Resilience is outclassed by powers in any other gameline that give you dots of Armor. Yes, they all give you a trait bonus too, but I think attributes are overpriced to begin with; it's just a couple dice, after all.<br /> <br /> So, because each is just one scaling power, I don't see it as the same as squishing Dominate, Nightmare, and Majesty together. It's more like if Dominate was just level 2 normally, but you had to buy more dots to have more than one individual mesmerized at once, you'd want to expand that out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Celerity in a street brawl would not be a masquerade breech as you literally move so fast the other people cant see you doing it. Perhaps if someone looked at some footage after.. oh wait, cant see a vampire on camera. it gives you a huge advantage in a foot chase, dodging attacks, ect. Being able to interrupt someone's action is huge.<br /> <br /> All the other ones give you a totally of 5 some where. I do not think yours should add any more than 5 total. perhaps if you spent it for celerity for the scene then 5 to defense for that scene. but not the other ones.. But it still does give you everything it would cost a normal vampire 50-55 exp+ 9-12xp depending on clans.<br /> <br /> As a story teller I would never be ok with something that would take someone else so much to achieve. If you would allow someone to take majesty, dominate, and nightmare and smash them into one, I would allow this But if you said no way to those 3. then why do you say yes to this one?<br /> </div> </div> </div>My reading of it is you see someone there and then they disappear and reappear elsewhere, which is pretty obviously supernatural. If you never stop to be seen once, sure, no breach, but then you're not in combat, you're just running by.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I went ahead and made some tweaks, based on your input. Maybe I did aim too high. I added a &quot;Physical Pool&quot; feature (Feel free to offer names for something cooler sounding), which is equal to your Somatics, and all your increases need to be allocated. I DID add an option so when you hit 5 dots, you may spend 2 XP to raise the physical pool itself, but still capping things at 5 dots, which I think is reasonable. So if you spend 15 +10 xp, you could have both Strength and Stamina at +5, for instance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also switched Aviation and Celerity's order around, since Celerity's likely a bit more powerful, even if flying has the cool factor. And lowered fortitude a bit; it no longer turns bashing to nothing, you need to use resilience if you want to get rid of any damage entirely. And as mentioned, changed Vigor so that way it lasts for Somatics turns, for 1 Vitae, instead of for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-27-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:00:34-07:00","id":958961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958932#post958932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, well, the basic idea is that every other discipline gives you 5 powers with their own uses, and each one is more potent than the last. The physical ones give you one power that gets better in a linear fashion with each dot, and a lot of them are underpowered even if you take it at a basis of, say, being the third dot of an unnamed discipline, in my opinion. Yes, +3 stamina is decent, but gaining 3 armor for 1 turn? That's very underwhelming to me.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that the comparison isn't wholly internal; I'm also comparing to other gamelines (I can't help it). Celerity is alright in the context of vampire, but is outclassed entirely by a werewolf in urhan, who can interrupt an unlimited number of times (if they have essence), for instance. Resilience is outclassed by powers in any other gameline that give you dots of Armor. Yes, they all give you a trait bonus too, but I think attributes are overpriced to begin with; it's just a couple dice, after all.<br /> <br /> So, because each is just one scaling power, I don't see it as the same as squishing Dominate, Nightmare, and Majesty together. It's more like if Dominate was just level 2 normally, but you had to buy more dots to have more than one individual mesmerized at once, you'd want to expand that out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My reading of it is you see someone there and then they disappear and reappear elsewhere, which is pretty obviously supernatural. If you never stop to be seen once, sure, no breach, but then you're not in combat, you're just running by.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I went ahead and made some tweaks, based on your input. Maybe I did aim too high. I added a &quot;Physical Pool&quot; feature (Feel free to offer names for something cooler sounding), which is equal to your Somatics, and all your increases need to be allocated. I DID add an option so when you hit 5 dots, you may spend 2 XP to raise the physical pool itself, but still capping things at 5 dots, which I think is reasonable. So if you spend 15 +10 xp, you could have both Strength and Stamina at +5, for instance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also switched Aviation and Celerity's order around, since Celerity's likely a bit more powerful, even if flying has the cool factor. And lowered fortitude a bit; it no longer turns bashing to nothing, you need to use resilience if you want to get rid of any damage entirely. And as mentioned, changed Vigor so that way it lasts for Somatics turns, for 1 Vitae, instead of for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You shouldnt compare werewolf abilities and vampire abilities or changeling abilities, because they are all unique creatures with unique abilities, banes, powers, strengths and weaknesses. You should compare your mechanics to other mechanics of similar power to gage if you are balanced or not. You shouldnt make a power to better a particular other splat power, as that wont balance your game.<br /> <br /> The other disciplines do offer 5 abilities but they are linear, they build upon each other. Idol is an extension of Awe. Auspex,( questions, better questions, questions about objects, flat out reading minds.. ect.. ) all build upon each other getting better each time. Protean does as well.<br /> <br /> Celerity as it is now gives you:<br /> 1 Defense Free<br /> 2 defense with fire arms Free<br /> 3 Move to the start of the init<br /> 4 interrupt turns<br /> 5 Movement speed<br /> 5<br /> the more exp you spend the more times you can do it and the better you are at it. <br /> <br /> For example Like Awe. everyone likes you a bit, hard to notice anything but you. a bit more exp and Idol you are a god in the room. <br /> <br /> Resilience as it is now gives you:<br /> 1 Stamina dots -free<br /> ~~ which gives you more health as well as adds to several different types of rolls ( so maybe like 6-10 additional bonuses )<br /> 2 Down grade damage for free. Aggravated damage equal to dots <br /> 3 so not only do you downgrade damage from fire and banes and whatever else for free, you now can ignore damage entirely plus 1 from mundane things<br /> 4 makes you nearly impossible to be staked<br /> 5 ignore damage entirely from banes and fire<br /> <br /> <br /> Vigor<br /> <br /> 1 Strength dots - free<br /> ~~ gives you bonus dice to all combat rolls ( not going to count these up either ) as well as a lot of mundane noncombat rolls.<br /> 2 better jumping rolls - free <br /> 3 Autodamage - makes called shots really easy. - in 3 different skills <br /> 4 lift or wield things that you shouldnt be able to. <br /> <br /> <br /> so each one of these gives you more than 5 things you can do with 1 dot... and you just get better at it with each subsequent EXP investment. <br /> <br /> <br /> If you were to list out the things you're new discipline does you are probably up in the 30s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:06:13-07:00","id":958964,"title":"","content":"As it is, this is now just solely getting back to the original point I don't want to get into. I disagree with your layout of how those disciplines progress and if it's balanced or does more/less than mental disciplines and protean, simply enough, and don't wish to make a big thing of it. But to summarize, just counting what number of things it does won't tell you if it's balanced or not; and yes, you have to balance in-game, but that doesn't mean you can't look at how a mechanic normally works among gamelines to know how potent it's considered overall (armor, for instance).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I did tweak the discipline, as mentioned, and think it's much more reasonable now, while still covering the issues I have with the original 3. If you don't have those issues with those 3, that's fine, and I've said all I'm going to on my disagreement with that. I'm still open to comments, mind, just along the lines of the frame of reference I've given here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-27-2016, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:52:52-07:00","id":959039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958964#post958964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ABut to summarize, just counting what number of things it does won't tell you if it's balanced or not;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then... why is this a core part of your justification and reasoning? You've repeatedly said that one of your problems is that the RAW physical Disciplines are &quot;one power&quot; that just gets better with each dot, but if you acknowledge that has nothing to do with balance, then it really shouldn't matter how many &quot;powers&quot; a Discipline gives you, but how much utility it gives you regardless of the way you count the &quot;powers.&quot;<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> For direct critiques:<br /> <br /> 1) The passive unlocks for Aviation and Celerity should be flipped. If Aviation is all about supernaturally fluid movement that lets you ignored athletics penalty, it makes more sense as a Defense booster. It's a lot easier to move out of the way of something if you're hovering and don't have to worry about footwork, and hovering gets in the way of things like delicate work. Celerity is focused on speed, but is a direct physical boost, making more sense with Dexterity.<br /> <br /> 2) Sneaking in Aviation-as-flight doesn't make sense as presented. Where does flying come from out of just making your body function at superhuman levels? Human bodies don't have &quot;hover&quot; organs to boost, and Vigor already covers jumping super far. The mechanics are pretty much pointless compared to just pumping Strength and Dexterity and combining it with Parkour; which also doesn't have issues with being overtly supernatural like flying does. You're not going to fly anywhere in a few turns that Vigor jumping and Celerity running isn't going to get you to just as fast/if not faster.<br /> <br /> 3) Having Resilience and Fortitude feels redundant. Fortitude feels tacked on as a 5th dot and just makes investing in Soak/Health based tactics more expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:11:12-07:00","id":959043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=958964#post958964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it is, this is now just solely getting back to the original point I don't want to get into. I disagree with your layout of how those disciplines progress and if it's balanced or does more/less than mental disciplines and protean, simply enough, and don't wish to make a big thing of it. But to summarize, just counting what number of things it does won't tell you if it's balanced or not; and yes, you have to balance in-game, but that doesn't mean you can't look at how a mechanic normally works among gamelines to know how potent it's considered overall (armor, for instance).<br /> <br /> Anyway, I did tweak the discipline, as mentioned, and think it's much more reasonable now, while still covering the issues I have with the original 3. If you don't have those issues with those 3, that's fine, and I've said all I'm going to on my disagreement with that. I'm still open to comments, mind, just along the lines of the frame of reference I've given here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if you make a list of all the disciplines and find that they roughly give you 5-10 different things you can do with them and you make a discipline that allows you to get 20-30 things. It would only be common sense that it is not balanced....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959039#post959039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then... why is this a core part of your justification and reasoning? You've repeatedly said that one of your problems is that the RAW physical Disciplines are &quot;one power&quot; that just gets better with each dot, but if you acknowledge that has nothing to do with balance, then it really shouldn't matter how many &quot;powers&quot; a Discipline gives you, but how much utility it gives you regardless of the way you count the &quot;powers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>that is exactly why I laid them out in a list of how many things they could do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Disciplines as their core are an extension of the beast. They take part of the beast and hone it to perfection. Majesty is clearly the seductive beast. Dominate is clearly the Competitive beast where Protean is the Monster or Nightmare is the monster.<br /> <br /> this what is this? This hones 5 different parts of the vampire. It gives you complete mastery over strength dexterity, stamina, healing and..... flight?<br /> <br /> flight seems like a protean celerity devotion or perhaps even vigor too<br /> <br /> Healing seems a coil of the dragon<br /> <br /> Again I ask of you. Would you as a story teller, let me take Majesty Nightmare and Dominate and smash them into 1 power? along with say summoning and cross=contamination for extra kicks? Heck would you even let me take an entire discipline and just make a merit equivalent to get it for cheaper EXP cost?<br /> <br /> If you say you are fine with that, then let this Discipline ride, But if you are not ok with that. ask yourself Why? Are they too powerful together? especially if you say. Made Idol permanent and allowed you to command reflexively..<br /> <br /> How do you justify putting 59-68 exp worth of stuff into something worth 15?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-27-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:08:51-07:00","id":959071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959039#post959039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then... why is this a core part of your justification and reasoning? You've repeatedly said that one of your problems is that the RAW physical Disciplines are &quot;one power&quot; that just gets better with each dot, but if you acknowledge that has nothing to do with balance, then it really shouldn't matter how many &quot;powers&quot; a Discipline gives you, but how much utility it gives you regardless of the way you count the &quot;powers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that just because the 1-5s have multiple effects doesn't mean they're balanced against the disciplines that progress normally. I guess I muddled my point in the wording there, but you're leaving out the fact that I also said that what the physical disciplines do is about equal to what a single, maybe level 3 or so singular discipline dot seems to do otherwise. That's the main issue, that it adds up to be worth a single dot in other disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For direct critiques:<br /> <br /> 1) The passive unlocks for Aviation and Celerity should be flipped. If Aviation is all about supernaturally fluid movement that lets you ignored athletics penalty, it makes more sense as a Defense booster. It's a lot easier to move out of the way of something if you're hovering and don't have to worry about footwork, and hovering gets in the way of things like delicate work. Celerity is focused on speed, but is a direct physical boost, making more sense with Dexterity.<br /> <br /> 2) Sneaking in Aviation-as-flight doesn't make sense as presented. Where does flying come from out of just making your body function at superhuman levels? Human bodies don't have &quot;hover&quot; organs to boost, and Vigor already covers jumping super far. The mechanics are pretty much pointless compared to just pumping Strength and Dexterity and combining it with Parkour; which also doesn't have issues with being overtly supernatural like flying does. You're not going to fly anywhere in a few turns that Vigor jumping and Celerity running isn't going to get you to just as fast/if not faster.<br /> <br /> 3) Having Resilience and Fortitude feels redundant. Fortitude feels tacked on as a 5th dot and just makes investing in Soak/Health based tactics more expensive. </div> </div> </div>1) I simply disagree there. Celerity seems to also affect reaction times and thing like that, so the defense boost makes more sense there, whereas aviation is unimpeded movement, which to me makes more sense for Dexterity.<br /> <br /> 2) The idea is that the vampiric body is supernatural and cares less about external force, which includes gravity in this context. It's meant to be a brief thing (thus the one turn per dot), not idle hovering or extended flight (you're better off with protean for the latter). Similar to the other shorter lasting abilities, it's meant to provide an immediate advantage in fast paced situations, rather than provide a new means of long term travel.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm open to other suggestions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959043#post959043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually if you make a list of all the disciplines and find that they roughly give you 5-10 different things you can do with them and you make a discipline that allows you to get 20-30 things. It would only be common sense that it is not balanced....</div> </div> </div> </div>As some off the cuff example going by how you laid things out, Dominate 1:<br /> 1) Force someone to perform simple tasks for you<br /> 2) Simply pacify someone by making them stand still and quiet.<br /> 3) Gain a brief ally by having someone attack an enemy, providing a combat advantage<br /> 4) Remove simple memories<br /> 5) Alter simple memories<br /> And yes, given you counted Resilience's armor as 3 different effects, each set of those do count as separate by the same guidelines, I think. So no, this doesn't do more than the mental disciplines already do.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, you're just repeating yourself, I'm not sure why you think that would convince me when I already said I disagree with that exact set of points, and don't want to discuss it further? I'm honestly confused, what do you get if you convince me the physical disciplines are stronger than I've experienced them to be firsthand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T23:06:36-07:00","id":959113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959071#post959071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was that just because the 1-5s have multiple effects doesn't mean they're balanced against the disciplines that progress normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's problematic to define the others as &quot;normally.&quot; We have four different progression patterns: the physical Disciplines, the non-physical in-Clan Disciplines, the sorcery Disciplines, and the Coils.<br /> <br /> This also doesn't really address the core point of why to bother with five separate powers in the non-physical in-Clan Discipline style is vital to addressing the issues with the utility level of them. Esp. since you actually need to sink a bunch of XP into Somatics to get the full use of it. It has a hidden extra 30 XP cost to max out. This somewhat blunts <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> issue with the amount of savings Somatics represents (though not entirely because it's still a major savings and it boosts Dexterity with the core physical Disciplines don't do directly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess I muddled my point in the wording there, but you're leaving out the fact that I also said that what the physical disciplines do is about equal to what a single, maybe level 3 or so singular discipline dot seems to do otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Well, you don't exactly make this a fair point. You're not going to accept any debate of this assumption as being true to the point of the thread, but then say that because I'm not addressing whether this assumption should be treated as valid my point is flawed.<br /> <br /> I will, however, point out that 2e removes a lot of the argument that different levels are actually an explicit measure of magnitudes of power. Five out of Clan Disciplines at 1 dot, cost the same XP as one out of Clan Discipline taken to 5. The assumption of utility is that each dot is roughly the same. That's why most of the non-physical in Clan Disciplines were made to be more internally reliant on their early dots. You can't forget about Dominate 1 if you want to use the higher levels even if the potency of the powers of the higher dots in vacuum is higher on paper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) I simply disagree there. Celerity seems to also affect reaction times and thing like that, so the defense boost makes more sense there, whereas aviation is unimpeded movement, which to me makes more sense for Dexterity. </div> </div> </div>Celerity is whatever you want it to be in Somatics. I'm pointing out that the thematic description of the two does not match the passive unlocks. Keep in mind that by having Dexterity unlocked like this, it's more than just combat that's being affected. If you can use Somatics to boost Dexterity, you're better at Dex + Crafts to make something delicate. Which is more important to that, unimpeded full body movement, or fine reaction times?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The idea is that the vampiric body is supernatural and cares less about external force, which includes gravity in this context. </div> </div> </div>This removes any coherent themes of the Discipline. Instead of pushing your innate physical power to supernatural extremes, it has become, &quot;a wizard did it.&quot; Any and every power can be justified by this logic. Aviation could be just as easily replaced with Hypnotism because the vampiric body is supernatural and can hypnotize people because it just can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similar to the other shorter lasting abilities, it's meant to provide an immediate advantage in fast paced situations, rather than provide a new means of long term travel. </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't actually address the mechanical stuff I proposed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As some off the cuff example going by how you laid things out, Dominate 1: </div> </div> </div>This is disingenuous. Vitalis pointed out specific mechanical impacts of each of the physical Disciplines, each of which has dozens of potential applications. Dominate 1 does one thing, even if you can put it to multiple uses. Vigor granting bonus Strength dots does one thing, even if you can put it to multiple uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:48:07-07:00","id":959208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959071#post959071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yes, given you counted Resilience's armor as 3 different effects, each set of those do count as separate by the same guidelines, I think. So no, this doesn't do more than the mental disciplines already do.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, you're just repeating yourself, I'm not sure why you think that would convince me when I already said I disagree with that exact set of points, and don't want to discuss it further? I'm honestly confused, what do you get if you convince me the physical disciplines are stronger than I've experienced them to be firsthand?</div> </div> </div> </div>As heavyarms stated I pointed out the specific mechanical impacts of each.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you think I listed Resilence armor 3 times and you think that's the same thing mechanically and state &quot; stronger than I have experienced&quot;, it leads me to believe my original assumption was correct and that you ( or your group) do not truly know how to use the physical disciplines. Each of the 3 things I listed was mechanically different.</span></span></span><br /> if you took just 1 dot of celerity and resilience and vigor you would only get 1 strength stamina and defense + some cool 1 time per scene use of stuff. With your 3 dot thing you would get +3 stamina,+ 3 strength, + 3 defense + entire scene use of each. Which is where my math came in Just that alone is 30-33 exp vs your 9 ( assuming you are making this &quot;in clan&quot; ).<br /> <br /> <br /> The specific mechanical impact of dominate 1<br /> 1 Mesmerize someone for a scene maybe long. ( give them 4 word commands )<br /> mechanically this is the ONLY thing you can do with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am repeating myself because the questions are ignored entirely.<br /> <br /> As far as what I get out of this? Nothing. Usually when people ask for help, people help not for something that they get, but for the sake of helping. It seems as though you do not want help, you wanted validation. Perhaps with the lack of help you are getting more people listened to &quot; If you think they are strong, this is not for you&quot; That in itself should speak to you. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Side note: In a duel if you walked up to someone with 4 dots of vigor and 1 celerity and you had 5 dots of any other discipline. ( min max on both ends + 2 blood potency so each could use their best discipline in 1 turn ) The physical vampire will just celerity to go first, vigor to get autodamage and stake you in 1 turn. all it would take is 1 success. the opponent would drop you before you could even Idol. And actually that happened to my 6BP Daeva with Majesty 5...... and it was another player at the table. I didnt even get a turn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-28-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:05:54-07:00","id":959222,"title":"","content":"I think the OPs issue is less balance of the original 3 physical disciplines and more that purchasing a new dot *feels* boring. Other disciplines make you feel like you are buying something new and exciting for each 3 or 4xp investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:34:09-07:00","id":959236,"title":"","content":"Oh. Note that I dont agree with this assertion, but I think it is the actual issue addressed by this new discipline. I can also definately see how someone would come to that conclusion. Physical disciplines get new things they can implicitly do, but not things they can explicitly do. They make who you are different, not what you can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:51:29-07:00","id":959245,"title":"","content":"If that's the case, then using the other's Discipline's template for each of the three physicals seems more logical than fusing them together and fill the gaps. It's been done in Masquerade a lot, maybe they can take inspiration from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:37:59-07:00","id":959269,"title":"","content":"I think his problem with it is that the physicals don't do anything new at different levels. You enhance the same attribute and can do the exact same special effects at level 1 that you can do at level 5, with only incremental improvements and increased frequency in a set time frame. Whereas when you get level 1 of Auspex, you get enhanced physical senses. But at level 4, not only has your enhanced senses improved incrementally, but you get a limited form of thought control (yanking out memories and forcing the victim to relive them) and projective telepathy. Two abilities you did not have at level 1.<br /> <br /> I don't believe physical disciplines are underpowered for THAT reason though because the respective attribute is enhanced permanently at no cost other than the initial XP cost. I'm personally not convinced paying for one additional damage downgrade or car chucking stunt is worth the xp price of a discipline by itself But since experience costs don't scale exponentially anymore and some disciplines are almost identical in regards to scaling as the physical disciplines maybe being underpowered isnt really the issue. Maybe it's the fact that investing in high ranks of the physicals is a questionable choice in terms of efficiency while nobody would blink an eye about someone zipping straight to 5 in the non physicals at the earliest opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:56:59-07:00","id":959284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959113#post959113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This removes any coherent themes of the Discipline. Instead of pushing your innate physical power to supernatural extremes, it has become, &quot;a wizard did it.&quot; Any and every power can be justified by this logic. Aviation could be just as easily replaced with Hypnotism because the vampiric body is supernatural and can hypnotize people because it just can.</div> </div> </div> </div> Weren't you just calling one of my arguments disingenuous below? You REALLY think a movement method is less physical than hypnotism? REALLY?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is disingenuous. Vitalis pointed out specific mechanical impacts of each of the physical Disciplines, each of which has dozens of potential applications. Dominate 1 does one thing, even if you can put it to multiple uses. Vigor granting bonus Strength dots does one thing, even if you can put it to multiple uses. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Resilience especially, how is 'gives armor, and it's better against mundane things than banes' the three distinct powers he claims? Dominate 1, at the very least, lets you command and alter memories, and there's no way you can tell me commanding and memory altering are the same but armor that works slightly differently depending on the source is.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm done responding to Vitalis anyway since he correctly pointed out that I don't want his help if it means repeating himself until I agree with him, and claiming I used the disciplines &quot;wrong&quot; when I used them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, as for new points brought in by others, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> i and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a>, the basic idea of it being boring is part of it, yes, but not the entirety of it. I keep coming back to resilience and the fact that the Armor is very underwhelming, but that's a huge one, really. As for the rest, yeah, they do all give attributes or defense, which might be worth it simply by how those are priced normally, but as I've said, attributes are already overpriced, and I also tried to compensate for this by switching to the Physical Pool in my discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this point, it does seem few people agree with the need for this discipline. While I still disagree with the physicial disciplines being balanced as it is, I think I'm done arguing. I really do hope someone enjoys Somatics and gets some use out of it, and if anyone else has input on the discipline itself and how it can be made better specifically, I'll respond to that of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:02:53-07:00","id":959390,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Aviation (basically, I imagine it as allowing Vampires to walk on walls, ceilings, that sort of creepy business - less full-on flying).<br /> <br /> I also like Fortitude's active effect to shrug off physical tilts.<br /> <br /> I am a bit iffy about the 'Physical Pool'. It feels a bit clunky in its presentation / mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:30:20-07:00","id":959483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959390#post959390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Aviation (basically, I imagine it as allowing Vampires to walk on walls, ceilings, that sort of creepy business - less full-on flying).<br /> <br /> I also like Fortitude's active effect to shrug off physical tilts.<br /> <br /> I am a bit iffy about the 'Physical Pool'. It feels a bit clunky in its presentation / mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure with a duration of a few turns it'd be along those lines, and the passive effect is meant to allow for &quot;wall-walking' and stuff by removing the penalties for climbing on slick surfaces and such.<br /> <br /> I hadn't considered shrugging off physicial tilts. That might be something worth looking into, I'll glance over that in a bit.<br /> <br /> As for the Physical Pool, do you have any suggestions to make it work better? I went to that to give the ability to raise traits for the different individual levels without getting too ridiculous in total amounts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tweaked Fortitude a bit, made it so you heal -faster- (agg damage can be healed in real time), and can also heal physical tilts and conditions, but you don't heal lethal and bashing any more efficiently, as I didn't want to just pile on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-28-2016, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:38:58-07:00","id":959525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959284#post959284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Weren't you just calling one of my arguments disingenuous below?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because it remains so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You REALLY think a movement method is less physical than hypnotism? REALLY? </div> </div> </div>Not less, equal. Both are not based in any actual physicality from the vampire, but hand-waved supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> If a vampire can be so agile that they can fly, why can't they be so alluring that they can put you in a hypnotic state? Both are taking &quot;vampires are magic&quot; as a bridge between, &quot;physical actions taken to supernatural levels,&quot; and, &quot;outright supernatural powers that are not extensions of physical abilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> If vampires could physically fly without Disciplines, and comparing it to being able to be hypnotic would be disingenuous. But that's not the case.<br /> <br /> Once you say, &quot;because the vampire's body is supernatural,&quot; as a reason for a power in the Discipline to allow a power that's not an application of normal physicality, you remove thematic coherence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I keep coming back to resilience and the fact that the Armor is very underwhelming, but that's a huge one, really. As for the rest, yeah, they do all give attributes or defense, which might be worth it simply by how those are priced normally, but as I've said, attributes are already overpriced, and I also tried to compensate for this by switching to the Physical Pool in my discipline. </div> </div> </div>All of which still fails to address the issue of why you're compressing these into one Discipline instead of just making the existing physical Disciplines better to what you consider should be their appropriate power level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At this point, it does seem few people agree with the need for this discipline. </div> </div> </div>The presentation and responses haven't really helped. It's very hard to be positive towards a &quot;critique my house rules thread,&quot; when it feels like the original poster is extremely reluctant to accept any actual criticism as valid, and feels the need to argue everything that isn't in agreement with the original formulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:03:59-07:00","id":959542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959525#post959525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The presentation and responses haven't really helped. It's very hard to be positive towards a &quot;critique my house rules thread,&quot; when it feels like the original poster is extremely reluctant to accept any actual criticism as valid, and feels the need to argue everything that isn't in agreement with the original formulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already made several changes based on critique. What bothers me is repeating the same thing over and over when I say &quot;I get what you're saying but disagree with your outlook&quot; (or the equivalent), as if it'd change my mind to repeat oneself. And then in your case, claiming a comparison is invalid and then doing something that's even more of a leap (even if you don't think it is, and PLEASE don't repeat your reasoning for why it's not again).<br /> <br /> And as for why do this instead of remaking the individual ones, it's simply what I decided to try out. Definitely also an option to remake each of the three. I mean, it's not like I'm writing the book here, this was very much a homebrew experiment, and something to use for those few that might agree with my view and approach.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And as to why I say &quot;Those who disagree with X shouldn't respond&quot; in some threads, it's because it seems to be a thing on this forum to go &quot;Hey I don't think that should exist!&quot; to homebrew when that doesn't help anything at all for anyone involved. It's not a thread asking if it should exist; clearly the person who wrote it thinks it should. Why do you need to convince them of that, when you can just not use it if you disagree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-28-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:22:44-07:00","id":959559,"title":"","content":"I think there are some solid ideas in this discipline; namely, the accelerated healing, immunity to physical tilts, and ability to supernaturally defy gravity and wall-walk (all of those things evoke a sense of supernatural horror to me while simultaneously being useful mechanically).<br /> <br /> I think you're trying to make this discipline so Vampires can potentially compete against Werewolves in physical altercations, would that be right (trying to get a sense of how powerful you want the discipline)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:32:37-07:00","id":959561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959559#post959559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are some solid ideas in this discipline; namely, the accelerated healing, immunity to physical tilts, and ability to supernaturally defy gravity and wall-walk (all of those things evoke a sense of supernatural horror to me while simultaneously being useful mechanically).<br /> <br /> I think you're trying to make this discipline so Vampires can potentially compete against Werewolves in physical altercations, would that be right (trying to get a sense of how powerful you want the discipline)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I wouldn't say it was a primary concern, but it definitely would make me happy to see vampires as competitive in the things they're meant to be naturally good at (being resilient and hard to kill, or supernaturally fast, for instance). But even if other splats didn't exist I'd still probably think the still-linear discipline design was underwhelming. If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> And honestly, I don't think it was a purposely made design choice to say vampires need to be weaker, slower, and less tough than other supernaturals. I think those disciplines were made, were cool, and then the developers took that and ironed out the limits for other splats which made them happen to be better at that thing because of it. So, sure, balance isn't a developer motive, but that doesn't mean you can't make those same sorts of changes to the splat that originally introduced the mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:38:20-07:00","id":959565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959284#post959284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Weren't you just calling one of my arguments disingenuous below? You REALLY think a movement method is less physical than hypnotism? REALLY?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not really. Resilience especially, how is 'gives armor, and it's better against mundane things than banes' the three distinct powers he claims? Dominate 1, at the very least, lets you command and alter memories, and there's no way you can tell me commanding and memory altering are the same but armor that works slightly differently depending on the source is.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm done responding to Vitalis anyway since he correctly pointed out that I don't want his help if it means repeating himself until I agree with him, and claiming I used the disciplines &quot;wrong&quot; when I used them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, as for new points brought in by others, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> i and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a>, the basic idea of it being boring is part of it, yes, but not the entirety of it. I keep coming back to resilience and the fact that the Armor is very underwhelming, but that's a huge one, really. As for the rest, yeah, they do all give attributes or defense, which might be worth it simply by how those are priced normally, but as I've said, attributes are already overpriced, and I also tried to compensate for this by switching to the Physical Pool in my discipline.<br /> <br /> <br /> At this point, it does seem few people agree with the need for this discipline. While I still disagree with the physicial disciplines being balanced as it is, I think I'm done arguing. I really do hope someone enjoys Somatics and gets some use out of it, and if anyone else has input on the discipline itself and how it can be made better specifically, I'll respond to that of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Buying attributes costs 4 Exp these Disciplines cost 3 or 4 exp and you get bonus stuff. You can be done responding and that is perfectly within your right to do so. i didnt say you use them wrong, but i really feel you dont understand them. I am not repeating myself until you agree, but I am repeating myself because it is apparent you are not understanding what is being said.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Resilience especially, how is 'gives armor, and it's better against mundane things than banes' the three distinct powers he claims?&quot;</i><br /> That statement is validation that you do not understand the mechanics behind the disciplines. <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Resilience as it is now gives you:<br /> 1 Stamina dots -free<br /> ~~ which gives you more health as well as adds to several different types of rolls ( so maybe like 6-10 additional bonuses )<br /> 2 Down grade damage for free. Aggravated damage equal to dots<br /> 3 so not only do you downgrade damage from fire and banes and whatever else for free, you now can ignore damage entirely plus 1 from mundane things<br /> 4 makes you nearly impossible to be staked<br /> 5 ignore damage entirely from banes and fire &quot;</i><br /> <br /> look at this<br /> 1You always automatically downgrade Aggravated damage equal to your dots, All the time for free, is Mechanically different than Downgrade any type of mundane damage + 1 for vitae which is also mechanically different than downgrade damage from banes equal to dots for vitae. All of those are mechanically different<br /> <br /> Dominate 1 has 1 mechanical effect.. You mesmerize the victim. 1 condition. Those are both facts not baseless &quot;claims&quot;<br /> You are aware you don't just get armor. You get all 5 of those mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Asking how you justify giving someone 50+ exp for 15 exp is not an invalid question.<br /> Asking if you would allow a player to take majesty, dominate and nightmare and put it into one discipline was fair was a valid question.<br /> Are you a player or a story teller?<br /> I also dont feel that anyone in this thread besides you has said this is a NEEDED thing. Sure it might feel boring but it is better than buying a dot in strength. That's what they are intended for.<br /> <br /> I am not sure of a single story teller that would let this fly in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-28-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:47:31-07:00","id":959567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959565#post959565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">look at this<br /> You always automatically downgrade Aggravated damage equal to your dots, All the time for free, is Mechanically different than Downgrade any type of mundane damage + 1 which is also mechanically different than downgrade damage from banes equal to dots. All of those are mechanically different<br /> <br /> Dominate 1 has 1 mechanical effect.. You mesmerize the victim. 1 condition. Those are both facts not baseless &quot;claims&quot;<br /> You are aware you don't just get armor. You get stamina</div> </div> </div> </div> You have a very different idea of what counts as mechanically different than I do, and we're going to leave that there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Asking how you justify giving someone 50+ exp for 15 exp is not an invalid question.<br /> Asking if you would allow a player to take majesty, dominate and nightmare and put it into one discipline was fair was a valid question.<br /> Are you a player or a story teller?<br /> I also dont feel that anyone in this thread besides you has said this is a NEEDED thing. Sure it might feel boring but it is better than buying a dot in strength. That's what they are intended for.<br /> <br /> I am not sure of a single story teller that would let this fly in a game. </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to justify it to you. That is not the point of this thread. It was never meant to be the point of this thread, but you hijacked it. I never said it was NEEDED, I said I disliked how it was now and wanted to create a new option. OPTION (like all homebrew inherently is). Even in the document itself, it's called out as an OPTION if you want kindred to be more physically powerful.<br /> <br /> I think you're clearly not understanding me either, given how you're misrepresenting what I've said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-28-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T17:02:32-07:00","id":959572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959567#post959567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You have a very different idea of what counts as mechanically different than I do, and we're going to leave that there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to justify it to you. That is not the point of this thread. It was never meant to be the point of this thread, but you hijacked it. I never said it was NEEDED, I said I disliked how it was now and wanted to create a new option. OPTION (like all homebrew inherently is). Even in the document itself, it's called out as an OPTION if you want kindred to be more physically powerful.<br /> <br /> So instead of repeating yourself, I would suggest you read through what I've said and see what I've actually written since you clearly are not understanding me either. I have gotten your points, you're just misunderstanding my response to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forgive me. I do not feel I hijacked your thread as every single one of my posts related to your original topic. You do not have to justify it to me, but you would have to justify it to your storyteller or the rest of your table and if you can't answer questions that are posed to you in the natural course of discussion, then it wouldnt sell very well. No one ever buys anything off of &quot;because it's magic&quot;<br /> <br /> We might have a different idea of what mechanical effects are, but if you do not think that is the &quot;dice rolling&quot; or &quot;condition receiving&quot; part of the game I would really suggest you look into that.<br /> <br /> This whole time I thought the point of this thread was for you to get help making something that would be effectively balanced in game and not break it. I am sorry If I was wrong on that assumption. You could clarify what your goal was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T17:19:01-07:00","id":959578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959572#post959572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me. I do not feel I hijacked your thread as every single one of my posts related to your original topic. You do not have to justify it to me, but you would have to justify it to your storyteller or the rest of your table and if you can't answer questions that are posed to you in the natural course of discussion, then it wouldnt sell very well. No one ever buys anything off of &quot;because it's magic&quot;<br /> <br /> We might have a different idea of what mechanical effects are, but if you do not think that is the &quot;dice rolling&quot; or &quot;condition receiving&quot; part of the game I would really suggest you look into that.<br /> <br /> This whole time I thought the point of this thread was for you to get help making something that would be effectively balanced in game and not break it. I am sorry If I was wrong on that assumption. You could clarify what your goal was?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree dice rolling and conditions are part of what mechanical effects are, what I meant is we have a different view of what a mechanically -distinct- power/effect is, is all. I see armor, even in different amount, as being the same. You don't. And visa versa for commanding/memory altering from the same condition. I don't think we need to discuss that further.<br /> <br /> I have answered many of your questions, but a large number of my answers were &quot;No I don't think it's the same&quot; or &quot;I disagree with that outlook&quot;. Given I'm not trying to convince you to let me use this at your table, that should be enough; I've made it clear at that point that I've seen your point and just have a different view. Which is fine. I'm not saying you're wrong. What I'm saying is that I don't agree with the points presented so won't change the discipline based on them. It's homebrew, so that should be the end of those given points.<br /> <br /> My goal was to make a more distinct, combined physical discipline that won't break the game, and I HAVE made some changes towards that end, such as the physical pool, among a few other tweaks. But the point of the thread is not to tell me if it should exist or not, I've already decided I wanted to create the option (and have) so that doesn't help. Nor is the point to convince people one way or another if it should be used or not (that's something for individuals and given tables to work out).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T20:28:04-07:00","id":959642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959542#post959542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already made several changes based on critique. What bothers me is repeating the same thing over and over when I say &quot;I get what you're saying but disagree with your outlook&quot; (or the equivalent), as if it'd change my mind to repeat oneself. And then in your case, claiming a comparison is invalid and then doing something that's even more of a leap (even if you don't think it is, and PLEASE don't repeat your reasoning for why it's not again).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're only making my case regarding the tone of your responses here.<br /> <br /> You're allowed to say, &quot;Your point is wrong because I said so!,&quot; and then, &quot;don't bother trying to defend your point because I already told you I said you're point was stupid and wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't want a fair discussion, which means I have no reason to actually think you want real criticism of your idea. You might be ready to mine a few ideas that you'll acknowledge were right, but it doesn't mean you're ready to have your ideas challenged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: And as to why I say &quot;Those who disagree with X shouldn't respond&quot; in some threads, it's because it seems to be a thing on this forum to go &quot;Hey I don't think that should exist!&quot; to homebrew when that doesn't help anything at all for anyone involved. </div> </div> </div>And this is a bullshit strawman I keep seeing these days.<br /> <br /> 1) If someone is really threadcrapping, it's against the rules. Report them instead of being more uncivil in your own posts thinking it will make discussions of your homebrew better.<br /> <br /> 2) If you want to direct the conversation in the thread away from specific topics, it's on you to provide guidance. It's a lot easier to keep things focus on, &quot;I'm looking for feedback on X, Y, and Z parts of my idea,&quot; then, &quot;here's my idea, what do you think about it?&quot; Esp. if you have no intention of listening to anything but stuff on X, Y, and Z.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T23:52:44-07:00","id":959694,"title":"","content":"The Physical pool is a bit cluncky. What if Somatics lets you improve your natural ability to boost your physical pools and healing? You can keep the Aviation power too. So first level improves your Strength boost, second your Stamina, third your Dexterity, Fourth your movility and Fifth your Healing. I'll think of specifics and post them later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T04:24:08-07:00","id":959746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959642#post959642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're only making my case regarding the tone of your responses here.<br /> <br /> You're allowed to say, &quot;Your point is wrong because I said so!,&quot; and then, &quot;don't bother trying to defend your point because I already told you I said you're point was stupid and wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't want a fair discussion, which means I have no reason to actually think you want real criticism of your idea. You might be ready to mine a few ideas that you'll acknowledge were right, but it doesn't mean you're ready to have your ideas challenged.<br /> <br /> And this is a bullshit strawman I keep seeing these days.<br /> <br /> 1) If someone is really threadcrapping, it's against the rules. Report them instead of being more uncivil in your own posts thinking it will make discussions of your homebrew better.<br /> <br /> 2) If you want to direct the conversation in the thread away from specific topics, it's on you to provide guidance. It's a lot easier to keep things focus on, &quot;I'm looking for feedback on X, Y, and Z parts of my idea,&quot; then, &quot;here's my idea, what do you think about it?&quot; Esp. if you have no intention of listening to anything but stuff on X, Y, and Z.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreeing isn't the same as calling an argument wrong or stupid, but this is otherwise too hostile in tone to be worth responding to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959694#post959694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Physical pool is a bit cluncky. What if Somatics lets you improve your natural ability to boost your physical pools and healing? You can keep the Aviation power too. So first level improves your Strength boost, second your Stamina, third your Dexterity, Fourth your movility and Fifth your Healing. I'll think of specifics and post them later.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like improving upon physical intensity and such? I had been considering that, but wasn't sure if it was too 'fleeting'. Still, I'm interested in seeing your specific ideas for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T06:55:21-07:00","id":959785,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of improving / house-ruling Physical Intensity.<br /> <br /> What if the dice bonus incurred by Physical Intensity was equal to the dots in Somatics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T07:28:14-07:00","id":959800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959746#post959746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like improving upon physical intensity and such? I had been considering that, but wasn't sure if it was too 'fleeting'. Still, I'm interested in seeing your specific ideas for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe, he meant the physical pools that Somatics gives, Physical intensity is an entirely different mechanic. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959785#post959785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of improving / house-ruling Physical Intensity.<br /> <br /> What if the dice bonus incurred by Physical Intensity was equal to the dots in Somatics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if a devotion was created something like:<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Celerity 3, Vigor 3, Resilience 3<br /> Reflexive 2<br /> <br /> For a scene double all physical intensity dice pools? ( you drop 4 vitae and get 16 dice. )<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> For a scene double the activated benefits from your physical disciplines for double the cost<br /> ( so you spend 2 vitae on Vigor and get 6 extra damage. It still seems extremely powerful, but it would eat your vitae fast enough where you would have to be choosy )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Devotion<br /> <br /> Celerity 2 and Protean 4 or Auspex 5<br /> Instant action<br /> Cost 1 vitae per scene<br /> Aviation<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:44:25-07:00","id":959840,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting thought; a devotion using Somatics as a prerequisite could be another angle.<br /> <br /> I know that the main concern with condensing three disciplines into one is that mechanics need to be condensed, too - and if it does too much, it may get a bit too bloated and confused - so pruning what you don't like, turning those 'extra' mechanics into devotions could be a good option.<br /> <br /> What do you think, guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:10:49-07:00","id":959854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline#post958831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case it need be said, if you don't think the physical disciplines are underpowered, then that's your right to think, but this thread isn't meant for you, just don't use the discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div> When people question your thread in terms of balance i thinks it's more about trying to understand your point of view than it is about trying to say you are or aren't wrong.<br /> <br /> i disagree with attributes being too expensive in terms of experience though. The for mortals the WOD describes 3 dots in something as above average, 4 being well above average and 5 being one of the best in the world. To me that means people can work their whole lives towards something and never make the 4th dot and even with a level of natural talent possibly never getting to the 5th. With that in mind even X5 per new dot seems way too generous to me. A mortal with 5 dots in Str is one of the strongest people on the planet while someone with 5 in Dex is one of the fastest.<br /> <br /> i understand Vampires should be way better than mortals but think raising attributes with experience should take just as long as anything else across the board, and since Vampires are immortal they have more time to do it as well as getting a free dot in one attribute to begin with. Also with enough blood potency you can even go higher than the 5th dot.<br /> <br /> Like someone else said guns and other sources only do bashing while Vampires also can't be knocked unconscious so they don't need to have the best of the best in terms of every other splat because in many ways they are the best but every splat should have its own set of strengths and weaknesses otherwise no one would ever bother playing anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:55:57-07:00","id":959874,"title":"","content":"Your Resilience is actually weaker than canon Resilience - sure, it's scene-long, but canon!Resilience doesn't give you armor. Canon!Resilience straight-up <i>subtracts damage</i>, which means that it ignores Armor Piercing and isn't subject to the &quot;armor can't reduce the damage dealt below 1 Bashing&quot; limit.<br /> <br /> Other than that... I dunno. I'm not sure I like it. I think I'll be sticking with the classic three + <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q3dMgL9v7Vryw-uvWzJ8meJrvvQDjGD6_vjJLPGCjso/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Subvolo</a> for now. They don't make the game math (and expected Discipline progression) cry bloody tears.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> As for Thorbes' idea...<br /> <br /> That's more Coil territory, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:12:35-07:00","id":959912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959746#post959746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagreeing isn't the same as calling an argument wrong or stupid, but this is otherwise too hostile in tone to be worth responding to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you still cling to this insipid double standard. I recall that you were the one resorting to tactics such as, &quot;call me X, well I'll just call you X!&quot; and caps shouting in lieu of actually making a civil point, not me.<br /> <br /> You get what you give man. Don't expect sunshine and roses when you're doing nothing but responding to criticism you invited with hostile defensiveness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959874#post959874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more Coil territory, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Redoing the physical Disciplines in model of the Coils instead of the non-physical in-Clan Disciplines could address some of the issues people have with them. It also has a nice feature of being able to more easily handle new additions, and an in-character hook as such a model of physical Disciplines might have inspired the Coils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T14:26:30-07:00","id":960016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seta143</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959854#post959854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When people question your thread in terms of balance i thinks it's more about trying to understand your point of view than it is about trying to say you are or aren't wrong.<br /> <br /> i disagree with attributes being too expensive in terms of experience though. The for mortals the WOD describes 3 dots in something as above average, 4 being well above average and 5 being one of the best in the world. To me that means people can work their whole lives towards something and never make the 4th dot and even with a level of natural talent possibly never getting to the 5th. With that in mind even X5 per new dot seems way too generous to me. A mortal with 5 dots in Str is one of the strongest people on the planet while someone with 5 in Dex is one of the fastest.<br /> <br /> i understand Vampires should be way better than mortals but think raising attributes with experience should take just as long as anything else across the board, and since Vampires are immortal they have more time to do it as well as getting a free dot in one attribute to begin with. Also with enough blood potency you can even go higher than the 5th dot.<br /> <br /> Like someone else said guns and other sources only do bashing while Vampires also can't be knocked unconscious so they don't need to have the best of the best in terms of every other splat because in many ways they are the best but every splat should have its own set of strengths and weaknesses otherwise no one would ever bother playing anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This .. this so much this. ^ <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959874#post959874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Resilience is actually weaker than canon Resilience - sure, it's scene-long, but canon!Resilience doesn't give you armor. Canon!Resilience straight-up <i>subtracts damage</i>, which means that it ignores Armor Piercing and isn't subject to the &quot;armor can't reduce the damage dealt below 1 Bashing&quot; limit.<br /> <br /> Other than that... I dunno. I'm not sure I like it. I think I'll be sticking with the classic three + <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q3dMgL9v7Vryw-uvWzJ8meJrvvQDjGD6_vjJLPGCjso/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Subvolo</a> for now. They don't make the game math (and expected Discipline progression) cry bloody tears.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> As for Thorbes' idea...<br /> <br /> That's more Coil territory, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that resilience subtracts damage flat out has been pointed out several times, yet continues to be called armor. Which is an entirely different mechanic. I find that so many people dont fully grasp everything that the mechanics allow you to do and they try to change them before they understand it. Hell, I would love to rewrite sorcery, but I havent got a clue how it works so I wouldnt try to change it with a 10 foot pole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959912#post959912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you still cling to this insipid double standard. I recall that you were the one resorting to tactics such as, &quot;call me X, well I'll just call you X!&quot; and caps shouting in lieu of actually making a civil point, not me.<br /> <br /> You get what you give man. Don't expect sunshine and roses when you're doing nothing but responding to criticism you invited with hostile defensiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>guilty as charged, but I really tried....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959912#post959912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redoing the physical Disciplines in model of the Coils instead of the non-physical in-Clan Disciplines could address some of the issues people have with them. It also has a nice feature of being able to more easily handle new additions, and an in-character hook as such a model of physical Disciplines might have inspired the Coils.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think at one point I suggested coils.<br /> <br /> For those who want Balance and the physical disciplines to be more Interesting I think that's a great way to go. Or some fun cheap devotions that add more unique stuff to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-29-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T14:56:12-07:00","id":960030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959874#post959874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Resilience is actually weaker than canon Resilience - sure, it's scene-long, but canon!Resilience doesn't give you armor. Canon!Resilience straight-up <i>subtracts damage</i>, which means that it ignores Armor Piercing and isn't subject to the &quot;armor can't reduce the damage dealt below 1 Bashing&quot; limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I did say in Somatics it's not &quot;true armor&quot; and called it &quot;effective armor&quot;, but forgot to point out that it can't be armor pierced. I was going for the same thing, I just keep saying &quot;Armor&quot; here because it pretty much is just armor immune to AP.<br /> <br /> I do like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a>' idea of having Physical Intensity be improved via a devotion, as another thing, though I'm still open to hearing more from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> when he clarifies what he had in mind. Though I'd probably have it replace the physical intensity bonus with (Discipline) rather than doubling it.<br /> <br /> As for redoing them as similar to Coils, that could be interesting too, though given it's more innate you'd need to decide how to represent Scales as something more intuitive (unless you JUST mean the Coil part, which could probably work).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959840#post959840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting thought; a devotion using Somatics as a prerequisite could be another angle.<br /> <br /> I know that the main concern with condensing three disciplines into one is that mechanics need to be condensed, too - and if it does too much, it may get a bit too bloated and confused - so pruning what you don't like, turning those 'extra' mechanics into devotions could be a good option.<br /> <br /> What do you think, guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm all for suggestions for trimming down bloat so long as the basic idea of what I'm doing here is preserved. I do want to hear any ideas for making the physical pool easier to use/understand, because I feel like that could work well once wittled down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=959912#post959912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you still cling to this insipid double standard. I recall that you were the one resorting to tactics such as, &quot;call me X, well I'll just call you X!&quot; and caps shouting in lieu of actually making a civil point, not me.<br /> <br /> You get what you give man. Don't expect sunshine and roses when you're doing nothing but responding to criticism you invited with hostile defensiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... not sure what you're referring to, now. I never called anyone anything, and I never shouted with caps. Sure, I capitalized one word here or there, to provide emphasis where text lacks a means to otherwise, but nothing like a sentence of all-caps shouting or whatever.<br /> <br /> At any rate, can we please just end this pointless argument?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 08-29-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:40:32-07:00","id":960092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958831-somatics-a-single-physical-discipline?p=960030#post960030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a>' idea of having Physical Intensity be improved via a devotion, as another thing, though I'm still open to hearing more from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> when he clarifies what he had in mind. Though I'd probably have it replace the physical intensity bonus with (Discipline) rather than doubling it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm all for suggestions for trimming down bloat so long as the basic idea of what I'm doing here is preserved. I do want to hear any ideas for making the physical pool easier to use/understand, because I feel like that could work well once wittled down.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean Physical intensity bonus with ( discipline? ) how would that work, mechanically? I am not sure what you are trying to say there? Physical intensity dice are equal to dots in... which discipline?<br /> <br /> I have given you suggestions on how to &quot;trim down the bloat&quot; Make a list of every MECHANICAL bonus that you get... and narrow it down to something more equivalent to the others. Each discipline in it's entirety allows you to Mechanically do 5-10 things. Make yours do Mechanically 5-10 things. <br /> <br /> And I don't mean how to use it in every scenario or what can be done with it once it is used, but I mean &quot;mechanically how to use it&quot; example; 1 vitae for this effect. Or this roll causes this condition. <br /> an example of fluff vs mechanic. Fluff. You can fly inside. You can fly outside. You can fly in the sunshine, you can Fly in the Darkness. You can propel through water like flying in the air. Mechanic: Vampire gains flight equal to their movement speed. <br /> <br /> <br /> When creating a unique homebrewed discipline I work back from a goal:<br /> <br /> <b>What do I want to achieve?</b><br /> <br /> How can I get there?<br /> <br /> Is it balanced in terms of Vampire and how they relate to each other.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}